{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"de1725a8459e6c63816d924f8480c92a93d1d84f8120ee8568726a20f754b45a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The Brain review is in, and it changes a few things:\n- **The memory-worker loop isn't fully fixed.** Brain PR #474 fixes your real, older store. But the reviewer built #474 and the loop the timing study reproduced still happens. That one has a different cause: two copies of the same session get treated as one ID, so the recorded fingerprint never matches the job's.\n- **New top item, which the original study missed:** read-only commands like `brief` take the exclusive write lock. If anything is writing, `brief` fails after 10.5 s. Writers hold the lock for 8–32 s.\n- **Realistic savings are smaller:** a cold setup goes from 105 s to about 65–80 s, not 45–55 s. Only one fix (−40% on history) was actually measured.\n\nIt also found three graph defects for my list:\n1. One query took 46 s narrowing down files even with a warm cache.\n2. `neighbors` misses calls made through function values.\n3. A duplicate symbol definition appears in the results.\n\nCorrecting the Brain list, then telling the Brain session it can start:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XPLjZkHJnruZx5SGw5HSra","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| 6 | **RESOLVED by brain PR #474')\nj=s.index('\\n',i)\nrow6=('| 6 | **SPLIT (corrected by the review):** brain PR #474 fixes the LEGACY-store variant (export aborted on a divergent cached transcript in a non-checkpoint-backed brain). '\n      'The loop this study reproduced is a DIFFERENT bug and survives #474 (reviewer built ef41d238; the same 3 jobs still go stale): a **session-ref collision**. '\n      'conversationSessionRef = sha(repo, branch, sid); an empty branch maps to \"main\" in both jobs and receipts, so a session with an unknown/ copy and a main/ copy shares one ref with two digests. '\n      'The receipt keeps the first copy, the job keeps the last, and they never match (conversation_session.go:40-52, memory_cmd.go:591-594/656-668, memory_receipts.go:180-187). '\n      'Fix: make jobs and receipts pick the same copy (fact e60bf39e: do not reject duplicate ids). memory_cmd.go:1162 is correct. '\n      'The first-MCP-brief lock wait (about 3.9 s) is separate and also survives #474. | memory worker, MCP | first MCP brief 3.9 s → about 0.5 s (lock part); 3/229 sessions never project | review: BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md |')\ns=s[:i]+row6+s[j:]\ns=s.replace('# Brain: proposed speed and efficiency fixes','# Brain: proposed speed and efficiency fixes\\n\\n> **Read BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md first.** It corrects several estimates (realistic cold setup is about 65-80 s, not 45-55 s), splits #6, refutes parts of #1/#7/#8, and adds M1: read paths take the exclusive write lock, so brief fails with brain_locked after 10.5 s while any writer holds it. M1 is the new #2 priority.',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['B2'].update(status='done', note='BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md landed. Corrected ranking: 1) export fan-out (+fail fast on partial clone); 2) M1: read paths take the exclusive write lock (brief fails at 10.5 s); 3) FTS full rebuild + page-cache spill; 4) historyTerms (measured -40%). #6 split: #474 fixes the legacy store; the reproduced loop is a session-ref collision. Realistic cold setup 65-80 s.')\ngseed=dict(id='G-seeds',lane='graph',title='Graph defects found by the Brain reviewer (feed into G1)',status='todo',owner='claude',source='proactive',note='(1) query preselect took 45.9 s on a cache HIT (53.2 s total) on entire-brain; (2) neighbors misses function-value references (openHistoryFTS reported no callers; history_fts.go:824 passes it as a value); (3) a spurious duplicate kind=tool def for historyTerms made impact ambiguous.')\nif 'G-seeds' not in T:\n    i=[t['id'] for t in d['tasks']].index('G1')\n    d['tasks'].insert(i, gseed)\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p)\nEOF","description":"Correct brain speedup row 6 and log graph defects"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018wCB1VnwqqAwptiaMDeWNC","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"A2: review landed — start Brain fixes; #6 split","message":"**A2 ping: BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md has landed.** Start the Brain fixes (C2). File: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md. I also updated BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md with a header pointing at the review and a corrected row 6.\n\nThe review ran on eb 318e4b05, read-only, with isolated stores and every claim re-checked. Three things you'll want first.\n\n## 1. #6 is a split, not fully fixed by #474\nThe reviewer **built #474 (ef41d238)**, ran a fresh setup (108 s, all components ok), and the **same 3 jobs still went stale** on the first worker pass (2c0a90c1, 5b6981d4, 77eee962).\n- Your fix is real, for the legacy store. #474 only touches transcript_cache_migration.go, so it applies only to a non-checkpoint-backed brain. That's your real store, and your end-to-end verification stands.\n- The timing study's stores are checkpoint-backed, with 0 cached files, so they hit a second cause, a **session-ref collision**:\n  - `conversationSessionRef = sha(repo, branch, sid)`, at conversation_session.go:40-52.\n  - An empty branch maps to \"main\" in both jobs (memory_cmd.go:591-594) and receipts (memory_receipts.go:180-182).\n  - A session with both an unknown/ copy and a main/ copy therefore gets one ref with two digests.\n  - The receipt keeps the first copy (memory_receipts.go:184-187), while the job keeps the last (supersede, memory_cmd.go:656-668). They never match.\n- All 3 stale sessions have an empty-branch entry plus a main entry, with receipts showing exchange_count 0.\n- **Caveat:** 019ff2ba has the same shape and is NOT stale. That's unexplained.\n- Fix constraint, from your own fact e60bf39e: don't reject duplicate ids; make jobs and receipts pick the same copy.\n- memory_cmd.go:1162 is still correct, as you said.\n\n## 2. Corrected ranking\n1. **#1 export fan-out, plus failing fast on partial clones.**\n   - \"The list already has the needed fields\" is REFUTED: the list has no branch and no session index.\n   - But local refs already hold 5,621/5,621 checkpoints, and persistent export loads the local snapshot anyway (export.go:311-318). So the fan-out is pure overhead.\n   - Fix: use the list for membership and the local snapshot for metadata; explain only non-local ids; fail fast.\n   - Today it burns about 4-5 h and then fails on the missing promisor blob.\n2. **M1, newly found: read paths take the EXCLUSIVE write lock.**\n   - CLI brief and MCP brain_brief fail with brain_locked at about 10.5 s whenever any writer holds the lock. Writers hold it 8-32 s.\n   - Chain: mcp.go:521 → retrieval_transport.go:147, with the timeout at brain.go:33.\n   - Your fact c71a4457 already saw this.\n3. **FTS full rebuild after every history change, plus page-cache spill.** Identity is the records fingerprint plus count; it does DROP/CREATE and a lazy rebuild. Fix #5 alone only moves about 5 s. `cache_size` is the cheap lever.\n4. **#2 historyTerms:** CONFIRMED, -40%, byte-identical.\n5. **#11 pattern corpus:** CONFIRMED and broader. It rebuilds after ANY fact change on any branch, for 18.7 s while holding the write lock.\n6. The #6 ref collision.\n7. #4 together with #3: -8-15 s combined, not 15-25.\n8. #7: parallelize; \"skip already indexed\" is REFUTED (already done).\n9. #8: keep ONLY a per-request graph-store memo. The filter-probe memo contradicts the security facts 1fbd341d and be31df57, and exp2's never-invalidated memo goes stale in MCP or the daemon.\n10. #10\n11. #9\n12. #13: `ENTIRE_BRAIN_GRAPH_BINARY` already exists, so it's worth about 25 ms.\n13. #12\n\nRealistic cold setup is about 65-80 s, not 45-55.\n\n## 3. Graph-side items it found (mine)\n- query preselect took 45.9 s on a cache hit.\n- neighbors misses function-value refs.\n- There's a spurious duplicate def for historyTerms.\n\nLogged on my board as G-seeds.\n\nP1 is still running, so A1 hasn't fired yet. Hold heavy work until I ping. Reading and editing code is fine meanwhile; only before/after timings and the re-index need the quiet machine."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
