T18:05:56.021Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"22f6de9e-8e17-4812-9743-951c2108d4e0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9248d1c4-b40a-485b-bea6-15e6c3184d7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KPqM4iQLfyFxGgQMbxStr9","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"2a460155-9d11-4bbf-9eac-50f10f70ed91","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:05:56.576Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md","oldString":"| C2 | brain | Work through `BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md` as corrected by the review. #6 is already resolved by #474. **cli re-index is the acceptance test** for fix #1, once G-partial lands too. |","newString":"| C2 | brain | Work through `BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md` in the review's corrected order (`BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`): #1 export fan-out + fail fast, M1 read paths off the exclusive lock, FTS rebuild + cache_size, #2, #11, #6 session-ref collision (#474 fixed only the legacy-store variant), then the rest. **cli re-index is the acceptance test** for fix #1, once G-partial lands too. |","originalFile":"# Semantic-layer plan: graph + brain\n\nThe one shared sequence for both sessions:\n- **graph**: the session `merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption`\n- **brain**: the session `fix-brain-initialization-ux`\n\nEdit your own lane's lines only, and announce changes by SendMessage. The todo board\n(`.claude/todo-board.json`) tracks the rows. This file is the order and the handoffs.\n\nRules that hold throughout:\n- nothing merges until all of this is finished; there is one merge handoff to Suhaan at the end\n- no approval asks\n- board writes go under the flock\n- ask before touching the other's repo or any shared state\n\n## Phase A: finish measuring (now)\n| # | Who | What | Done when | Hands off |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | graph | Graph timing study P1 finishes (latest main d4a0c186) | `devenv-worktrees/timing/PROCESS-MAP.md` exists | graph pings brain: **heavy I/O may start** |\n| A2 | graph | Adversarial review of the Brain speed list | `devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` exists | graph pings brain: **start Brain fixes (C2)** |\n\nUntil A1 ends, neither session runs heavy disk or CPU work (full suites, re-index, large deletes). The timing is\nbeing measured.\n\n## Phase B: refresh, after A1. One heavy job at a time, in this order.\n| # | Who | What | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | graph | Run the held deletions: 123 stale or dirty clones (79.9 GB, `devenv-worktrees/cleanup-audit/delete-check.txt`, minus `Documents/Coding/entire-judge`), Ollama models, old Rust toolchains, **plus the stray Brain stores**: `gh/entireio/entire-sem` (the old name of entire-graph) and about 25 hackathon/demo repos | Keep the 4 that matter: entire-brain, entire-graph, entiredb, cli (about 17.5 GB). Facts stay backed up. Ping brain when done. |\n| B2 | brain | Re-index Brain on **3 repos, in order: entire-graph (canary) → entire-brain → entiredb** | **cli moves to Phase C** as the acceptance test. It needs both Brain fix #1 (export/explain, about 4-5.6 h today) and graph G-partial (graph refuses `index --head` on the partial clone). |\n| B3 | graph | **graph runs `entire graph setup` ONCE per repo, with both products active, never concurrently**, then prewarms `index --head` on the same 3 repos | One setup writes the combined guide for graph+brain (`renderActivation`, activation.go:26). Two interleaved setups can leave a duplicate activation marker, which `parseActivation` (activation.go:42) refuses until it is hand-repaired. brain does not call `entire brain setup` on shared repos. Setup rewrites tracked CLAUDE.md blocks in main checkouts; nothing is committed. |\n| B4 | graph | Delete the dev-mods `todo-live` copy before the next restart | The permanent `todo-board` mod carries the band. |\n\nThe real Brain store (`~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos`, about 37 GB, facts backed up 141/141) is\ndeleted **only after** brain lands the export/explain speedup (Brain fix #1) and a rebuild on one repo is proven to\ntake minutes. brain owns that call.\n\n## Phase C: fix loops, in parallel lanes\n| # | Who | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| C1 | graph | G1: graph fix list with estimated savings, from P1. G2: adversarial review. G3: work through it, one PR per fix, each with a before/after timing and mutation-proven tests. |\n| C2 | brain | Work through `BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md` as corrected by the review. #6 is already resolved by #474. **cli re-index is the acceptance test** for fix #1, once G-partial lands too. |\n| C3 | graph | Graph items that block Brain: **G-partial** (graph refuses `index --head` on partial clones, so Brain's cli semantic index fails), per-commit graph store rebuild (brief drops code context after each commit), host dispatch overhead of about 30-50 ms per call |\n| C4 | graph | #142 rescope: drop `--max-seconds` and the partial path; keep cancellation, `refuseTruncatedSnapshot` in all 3 writers plus its test, the filterActive guard, and the TestTF142R6 allowlist entry |\n| C5 | graph | Tune the graph arm of the adoption counter (brain-memory mod, built by brain) against `devenv-worktrees/fresh-env` (repo outside $HOME) |\n\n**Measuring windows (agreed; applies to both sessions, brain first).** A fix's before/after timing needs a quiet machine. Before measuring, post a board row\n`measuring: <what>, until <time>` in your lane and message the other session. The other session holds heavy work\nuntil it clears.\n\n## Phase D: close out\n| # | Who | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | graph | Fill the Graph tab of https://claude.ai/artifact/1YbGGd5Gk19omne4PyU7h1 and update the Brain tab with the fixes that landed |\n| D2 | both | Fresh-env usage check on the final builds (graph + brain), re-baselined after #474 |\n| D3 | graph | Close graph PRs superseded by what landed (git ancestry checked first) |\n| D4 | both | **One merge handoff to Suhaan**: every open PR in both lanes, in dependency order, CI and findings state for each |\n| D5 | Suhaan | `/compact` (graph says when) |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":38,"oldLines":7,"newStart":38,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | # | Who | What |"," |---|---|---|"," | C1 | graph | G1: graph fix list with estimated savings, from P1. G2: adversarial review. G3: work through it, one PR per fix, each with a before/after timing and mutation-proven tests. |","-| C2 | brain | Work through `BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md` as corrected by the review. #6 is already resolved by #474. **cli re-index is the acceptance test** for fix #1, once G-partial lands too. |","+| C2 | brain | Work through `BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md` in the review's corrected order (`BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`): #1 export fan-out + fail fast, M1 read paths off the exclusive lock, FTS rebuild + cache_size, #2, #11, #6 session-ref collision (#474 fixed only the legacy-store variant), then the rest. **cli re-index is the acceptance test** for fix #1, once G-partial lands too. |"," | C3 | graph | Graph items that block Brain: **G-partial** (graph refuses `index --head` on partial clones, so Brain's cli semantic index fails), per-commit graph store rebuild (brief drops code context after each commit), host dispatch overhead of about 30-50 ms per call |"," | C4 | graph | #142 rescope: drop `--max-seconds` and the partial path; keep cancellation, `refuseTruncatedSnapshot` in all 3 writers plus its test, the filterActive guard, and the TestTF142R6 allowlist entry |"," | C5 | graph | Tune the graph arm of the adoption counter (brain-memory mod, built by brain) against `devenv-worktrees/fresh-env` (repo outside $HOME) |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6d11facd-5610-402b-9d59-d92012b3d37e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"22f6de9e-8e17-4812-9743-951c2108d4e0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"cfe0bfe6-8d1e-4534-bab7-9673f6a149c3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9248d1c4-b40a-485b-bea6-15e6c3184d7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014rCMiKEuSXiP29GgEvV3RX","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"9e644bbf-aa87-4951-92d2-bda57384c414","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:05:56.672Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md","oldString":"105 s → roughly 45-55 s: −17.7 s from #2, −10 s from #3, −15-25 s from #4, plus #7 on re-runs. The first brief would be about\n0.6 s instead of 6.4 s, the first MCP brief about 0.5 s instead of 3.9 s, and cli setup would finish at all.","newString":"~~105 s → roughly 45-55 s~~. **Corrected by the review: about 65-80 s.** Only #2 (−17.7 s) was measured; #3 and #4 together\nare −8-15 s, not −25-35 s, because their cost is page-cache spill, not parsing. The first brief is about 0.6 s only if the FTS\nstops being fully rebuilt after every history change (#5 alone relocates the cost). The first MCP brief drops to about 0.5 s\nonly with M1 fixed. cli setup finishes at all once #1 lands (explain only non-local ids; fail fast on a partial clone).","originalFile":"# Brain: proposed speed and efficiency fixes\n\n> **Read BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md first.** It corrects several estimates (realistic cold setup is about 65-80 s, not 45-55 s), splits #6, refutes parts of #1/#7/#8, and adds M1: read paths take the exclusive write lock, so brief fails with brain_locked after 10.5 s while any writer holds it. M1 is the new #2 priority.\n\nMeasured 2026-10-24 on entire-brain `main` 318e4b05 (= installed v0.2.0-nightly), with the graph at d4a0c186.\nIsolated store, no daemon. Quiet-machine numbers (load 7-10).\nFull process maps: `PROCESS-MAP.md`. Raw data: `results/`. Profiles: `profiles/`, `results/pprof/`.\n\n**Status: proposals only.** Per the user, no Brain fixes are being made now. Two were prototyped on scratch branches\n(`eb-exp1`, `eb-exp2`) to measure them, and nothing was committed.\n\n## Where the time goes today\n\n| Process | Time | Dominant step |\n|---|---|---|\n| setup, `cli` (5,621 checkpoints) | **never finishes**, projected 3.9-5.6 h | 5,621 sequential `entire checkpoint explain <id>` calls, 2.5-3.6 s each (99.99% subprocess wait) |\n| setup, entire-graph, cold | 105 s, 1.45 GB RSS | history index 52.4 s (50%), pattern layer 31.6 s (30%), semantic 10.3 s, entity index 7.4 s |\n| setup re-run, nothing changed | 17.3 s | entity index 10.6 s (re-runs 10 `graph diff` every time) |\n| setup re-run after one `remember` | 37 s | pattern corpus rebuilt, 21.5 s |\n| first `brief` after setup | 6.4 s, 609 MB | lazy history search-index build, 5.37 s (sqlite write) |\n| warm `brief` | 610 ms | status 383 ms, graph context 127 ms, history rank 67 ms |\n| first `brain_brief` over MCP | 3.9 s | waits about 3.5 s on a background worker's write lock |\n| `doctor` | 1.94 s, 788 MB RSS | decodes all 158k history records |\n| `status` | 445 ms | |\n| `distill --dry-run` | 6.7 s | CPU over 1.27 GB of transcripts |\n| recall / query / search | 72-128 ms | fine |\n| MCP tool list | 31.8 KB (~8k tokens) per agent session | 32 tool schemas |\n\n## Proposed fixes, ranked by user-visible saving\n\n| # | Fix | Where | Saving | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Stop the per-checkpoint host-CLI call during export.** The list call (5.8 s) already returns session ids, agent and date for all checkpoints. Use those fields, or a batch call, an immutable per-checkpoint cache, bounded parallelism, or the local fast path for local checkpoints. | session export (repos with a separate checkpoint remote, e.g. cli) | **hours: from \"never finishes\" to finishing.** About 4-5.6 h becomes seconds to minutes. | timing log: 336 calls in 1,198 s; 2.5-3.6 s each |\n| 2 | **`historyTerms` normalizes the whole text once per keyword**, up to 26x. Normalize once, then match. | history index | **history 52.4 s → 31.5 s (−40%), setup −17.7 s.** Measured, with identical output (157,977 records, same sha256). | CPU profile: `historyTerms` 18.2 s, of which `normalizeHistorySearchText` 16.3 s |\n| 3 | **Typed JSON decode** instead of untyped maps, and stream the records instead of holding them all in memory. | history index | estimated −10 s CPU and a much smaller heap than the 1.45 GB peak | profile: `json.Unmarshal` 14.2 s; `runtime.madvise` 11.4 s; GC 8.5 s |\n| 4 | **Parse each transcript once** for history, episodes and corpus. Today it is parsed three times. Write the staging DB with sqlite fast-write pragmas and one transaction. | pattern layer + history | **estimated 15-25 s** off a cold setup | profile: second and third parse 11 s + 6.2 s CPU; about 13 s off-CPU in sqlite, one transaction per session |\n| 5 | **Build the history search index during setup**, not lazily on the first brief. | brief | **first brief 6.4 s → about 0.6 s** | profile: `openHistoryFTS` 6.49 s |\n| 6 | **SPLIT (corrected by the review):** brain PR #474 fixes the LEGACY-store variant (export aborted on a divergent cached transcript in a non-checkpoint-backed brain). The loop this study reproduced is a DIFFERENT bug and survives #474 (reviewer built ef41d238; the same 3 jobs still go stale): a **session-ref collision**. conversationSessionRef = sha(repo, branch, sid); an empty branch maps to \"main\" in both jobs and receipts, so a session with an unknown/ copy and a main/ copy shares one ref with two digests. The receipt keeps the first copy, the job keeps the last, and they never match (conversation_session.go:40-52, memory_cmd.go:591-594/656-668, memory_receipts.go:180-187). Fix: make jobs and receipts pick the same copy (fact e60bf39e: do not reject duplicate ids). memory_cmd.go:1162 is correct. The first-MCP-brief lock wait (about 3.9 s) is separate and also survives #474. | memory worker, MCP | first MCP brief 3.9 s → about 0.5 s (lock part); 3/229 sessions never project | review: BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md |\n| 7 | **Run the 10 `graph diff` calls in parallel or as one batch**, and skip commits already indexed. | entity index | **6-8 s off every warm setup and watch tick** | 10 sequential calls, 7.4-10.6 s |\n| 8 | **Cache the git filter probe and the `graph store` result per process.** brief calls `graph store` twice. | brief, status, small-repo setup | **brief −26% (610 → 449 ms), status −48% (445 → 234 ms).** Measured, identical output. Probe is 19% of small-repo setup. | prototype `eb-exp2` |\n| 9 | **Run the status probes in parallel with graph context** in brief. | brief | estimated 100-250 ms | estimate only |\n| 10 | **doctor reads health metadata** instead of decoding the full index. | doctor | **about −1.5 s and −750 MB** | profile: `loadBrainHistoryIndex` 1.10 s, `decodeBrainHistoryIndex` 0.91 s |\n| 11 | **Pattern corpus: update incrementally** after a `remember`, instead of rebuilding it. | setup re-run | about −20 s on the next re-run (37 s → 17 s) | re-run after remember: corpus rebuilt 21.5 s |\n| 12 | **Trim the MCP tool list** (descriptions, rarely used tools behind one dispatcher). | every agent session | about 8k tokens of context per session | tools/list = 31.8 KB |\n| 13 | **Host dispatch overhead** of about 30-50 ms per `entire graph` call (Brain → host CLI → graph). Call the graph binary directly when it is known. | brief, setup | about 30-50 ms per graph call | shim timings |\n\n## Bugs found while measuring (not speed, but user-visible)\n\n- **cli semantic index fails**: the graph refuses `index --head` on a partial-clone repo, and the real `devenv/cli` has the same configuration.\n- **No-egress session export fails** on the partial clone (missing blobs).\n- **Every new commit silently drops code context from brief** (\"search store not built for this commit\") until the graph store is rebuilt.\n- **The memory-worker retry loop** above (#6) runs forever-ish in the background.\n\n## If these were all done (rough, cold setup on entire-graph)\n\n105 s → roughly 45-55 s: −17.7 s from #2, −10 s from #3, −15-25 s from #4, plus #7 on re-runs. The first brief would be about\n0.6 s instead of 6.4 s, the first MCP brief about 0.5 s instead of 3.9 s, and cli setup would finish at all.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":53,"oldLines":5,"newStart":53,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## If these were all done (rough, cold setup on entire-graph)"," ","-105 s → roughly 45-55 s: −17.7 s from #2, −10 s from #3, −15-25 s from #4, plus #7 on re-runs. The first brief would be about","-0.6 s instead of 6.4 s, the first MCP brief about 0.5 s instead of 3.9 s, and cli setup would finish at all.","+~~105 s → roughly 45-55 s~~. **Corrected by the review: about 65-80 s.** Only #2 (−17.7 s) was measured; #3 and #4 together","+are −8-15 s, not −25-35 s, because their cost is page-cache spill, not parsing. The first brief is about 0.6 s only if the FTS","+stops being fully rebuilt after every history change (#5 alone relocates the cost). The first MCP brief drops to about 0.5 s","+only with M1 fixed. cli setup finishes at all once #1 lands (explain only non-local ids; fail fast on a partial clone)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6d11facd-5610-402b-9d59-d92012b3d37e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cfe0bfe6-8d1e-4534-bab7-9673f6a149c3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
