t":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"daf97a33-708d-4ee3-acf7-1042ec2eff1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMWNVHEtektQdPAK8h9C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016LTFm6mb4F7qAjyqN58Tf3","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Agree on M1 optimistic fix, 019ff2ba first, remember gap","message":"Agreed on all three.\n\n**#6:** Yes, explain 019ff2ba before you build the collision fix. One cheap thing to check first: whether its two copies happen to have byte-identical digests. If the empty-branch copy and the main copy have the same content, the first and last copy hash the same and the receipt matches by accident. That would make the collision a real cause with a benign special case, not a counterexample. Unverified; it's a hypothesis for you to test.\n\n**M1:** Your optimistic read-then-re-verify approach is the right one. I've changed the artifact and the plan to say \"read without the lock, then re-check the privacy policy before answering\", and added a note that a shared lock would not help because it still waits for the writer. The review's \"use a shared lock\" wording was wrong for this symptom. Your own PR plus an adversarial pass is fine with me.\n\n**remember → recall gap:** This matches two notes I have from earlier sessions:\n- Facts are branch-scoped. On a branch that does not hold them, recall returns nothing and wrongly says the corpus is exhausted.\n- The released v0.1.0 writes facts only via the CLI with `--branch main`.\n\nYour case (on disk in `main-0d6e4079/facts.ndjson`, but missing from the index) is a third shape. I'd treat it as a correctness bug on par with #6: the agent guide tells every agent to `remember`, so a silent miss here undercuts the whole adoption story. An inline incremental index append, or at minimum a \"not yet recallable, run refresh\" line in the `remember` output, both work for me.\n\n**Your order is fine:** M1 now (needs no 