{"parentUuid":"9558d88e-c124-41d4-80ca-75db47cdecae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMWv5ZN2Dmz8hBtt48PK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While the reviewer works, I'm filling the artifact's Graph tab with the timing data. That's docs-only work, which is fine during the Brain session's window."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3701,"cache_read_input_tokens":209635,"output_tokens":5099,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":842},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3701,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5099,"cache_read_input_tokens":209635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3701},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c6ab0acd-450c-4a4a-8387-a9811ba21e2b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMWv5Em9yCCc1ZHsBATY","requestRef":"eabda28c-c1de-4fe9-9667-1002a718843d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"25c09ff2-3ea6-48ad-a7ea-dbfae38c3457","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:14:14.140Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"25c09ff2-3ea6-48ad-a7ea-dbfae38c3457","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMWv5ZN2Dmz8hBtt48PK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R2ReeUGCfsnG5s7BDyH5pk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('    <div class=\"pending\">\\n      <h3>Still being measured</h3>')\nj=s.index('</section>',i)\ngraph_html='''    <div class=\"callout\"><b>One exact-name search took 6 minutes.</b> Searching entire-graph for a bare identifier (<span class=\"mono\">SearchRepository</span>) took 355 s, almost all of it in one <span class=\"mono\">git grep</span> with a regex alternation over the whole commit. The same route costs 8 s on cli, where a fixed-string search takes about 40 ms.</div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Overall the new build is much faster after the first call.</b> Warm queries are 2–6x faster. Cold builds are about 1.8x faster and use half the memory. A second worktree reuses the cache. The old build hangs on every graph-building command on the entire-graph repo itself. Two things got slower: the first query in a repo, and warm <span class=\"mono\">def</span>/<span class=\"mono\">neighbors</span>/<span class=\"mono\">impact</span>.</div>\n\n    <h2>Where the time goes</h2>\n    <div class=\"procs\" id=\"graph-procs\"></div>\n\n    <h2>New build vs the 2026-09-18 build (cli repo)</h2>\n    <div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n      <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Old</th><th>New</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Cold index</td><td class=\"num\">20.96 s</td><td class=\"num\">11.23 s</td><td>1.9x faster</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>First query in a repo (cold)</td><td class=\"num\">14.16 s</td><td class=\"num\">16.23 s</td><td><b>slower</b>: builds the complete graph up front</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Warm query, same question</td><td class=\"num\">5.64 s</td><td class=\"num\">3.06 s</td><td>1.8x faster</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Warm query, new question</td><td class=\"num\">16.44 s</td><td class=\"num\">2.63 s</td><td>6.3x faster (old missed the cache)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Query from a second worktree</td><td class=\"num\">13.69 s</td><td class=\"num\">2.42 s</td><td>5.7x faster (cache shared)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Exact-name query</td><td class=\"num\">14.77 s</td><td class=\"num\">11.77 s</td><td>8 s of it is one git grep</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Warm def / neighbors / impact</td><td class=\"num\">0.45 s</td><td class=\"num\">0.66 s</td><td><b>slower</b>: re-sorts history on every cache hit</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Warm edges / snapshot</td><td class=\"num\">20.3 s</td><td class=\"num\">0.29–0.56 s</td><td>36–71x faster (old rebuilt every time)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Three cold queries at once</td><td class=\"num\">16.50 s</td><td class=\"num\">17.25 s</td><td>about the same wall time, but 1 build instead of 3</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Peak memory, cold index</td><td class=\"num\">1,004 MB</td><td class=\"num\">432 MB</td><td>less than half</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>stats (7 days)</td><td class=\"num\">2.63 s</td><td class=\"num\">3.14 s</td><td>slightly slower</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table></div>\n    <p class=\"note\">entire-brain and entiredb show the same pattern. The optional sqlite search store makes the cache 18–27x larger, and it is not faster on every repo.</p>\n\n    <h2>Proposed fixes, by saving</h2>\n    <p class=\"note\">Ranked by saving per working session (one cold query plus about ten warm commands). A reviewer is checking each against the source now. Each fix becomes its own PR, with an old/new timing taken on a quiet machine and a check that output is unchanged.</p>\n    <div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Fix</th><th>Saving</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody id=\"graph-fixes\"></tbody>\n    </table></div>\n\n    <h2>Wrong answers found</h2>\n    <ul class=\"tight\">\n      <li><span class=\"mono\">neighbors</span> misses a function passed as a value, so it reported no callers for one that has them.</li>\n      <li>A spurious duplicate definition makes <span class=\"mono\">impact</span> ambiguous for one symbol.</li>\n      <li>The graph refuses to index a partial clone (<span class=\"mono\">blob:none</span>), which also breaks Brain's code index on the cli repo.</li>\n    </ul>\n  '''\ns=s[:i]+graph_html+s[j:]\ns=s.replace('<span>Compared with <b>the 2026-09-18 nightly</b></span>','<span>Compared with <b>the 2026-09-18 nightly</b></span><span>3 runs each, median; machine partly loaded by other work</span>',1)\njs='''const GRAPH = [\n  { name: \"Exact-name query, entire-graph repo\", total: \"355 s\", slow: true, note: \"One git grep with a regex alternation over the whole commit (the alias route). 338–370 s across 3 runs.\",\n    steps: [[\"git grep preselect\", 345000, \"a\"], [\"Everything else\", 10000, \"e\"]] },\n  { name: \"First query in a repo (cold), cli\", total: \"17.6 s\", slow: true, note: \"Scans file contents to pick candidates, then builds the complete graph anyway.\",\n    steps: [[\"Preselect content scan\", 4220, \"a\"], [\"Complete build\", 11100, \"b\"], [\"Rank\", 970, \"c\"], [\"Save complete cache\", 460, \"d\"], [\"Selective view\", 350, \"d\"], [\"Other\", 500, \"e\"]] },\n  { name: \"Cold index, cli\", total: \"11.7 s\", note: \"Only 2.2 cores busy on average: the ordered pipeline admits 8 files, so one slow file stalls the rest. Regex is 54% of the CPU.\",\n    steps: [[\"Per-file scan\", 7080, \"a\"], [\"Route passes (one thread)\", 1750, \"b\"], [\"Parse\", 750, \"c\"], [\"Similarity\", 590, \"d\"], [\"Save\", 550, \"d\"], [\"Sort, prepare, other\", 980, \"e\"]] },\n  { name: \"Warm query, cli\", total: \"2.9 s\", note: \"Ranking dominates. Each new question also writes a derived cache file.\",\n    steps: [[\"Rank\", 1270, \"a\"], [\"Load cache\", 630, \"b\"], [\"Save selective view\", 500, \"c\"], [\"Select from full\", 230, \"d\"], [\"Preselect\", 180, \"d\"], [\"Other\", 90, \"e\"]] },\n  { name: \"Warm def / neighbors / impact, cli\", total: \"0.66 s\", note: \"Slower than the old 0.45 s: each cache hit re-reads history and re-sorts every relation.\",\n    steps: [[\"Decode cache\", 350, \"a\"], [\"Re-sort history\", 180, \"b\"], [\"Other\", 130, \"e\"]] },\n];\nconst GFIXES = [\n  [\"Exact-name search: use a fixed-string git grep or the cached term index instead of a regex alternation over the commit\", \"8 s (cli) to about 6 min (entire-graph) per bare-name search\", \"big\", \"timing\"],\n  [\"Let the indexing pipeline run ahead of a slow file (wider ordered window)\", \"cold index −29% (cli) to −36% (brain); every cold command\", \"meas\", \"local patch, identical output\"],\n  [\"Skip the preselect content scan on a cold query when the complete build follows anyway\", \"−4.2 to −6.3 s per first query\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n  [\"Stop re-sorting history on every cache hit; merge in place and remember it per commit\", \"−0.15 to −0.2 s per warm command; fixes the slowdown\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n  [\"Stop writing the derived selective view on every new warm question\", \"−0.5 to −0.7 s per warm query\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n  [\"Replace per-pattern regex in relation extraction with one shared pass\", \"−2 to −4 s per cold build\", \"est\", \"CPU profile\"],\n  [\"Run the HTTP route passes inside the parallel scan\", \"−1 to −1.7 s per cold build\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n  [\"Precompute ranking token variants\", \"−0.5 to −1 s per warm query\", \"est\", \"CPU profile\"],\n  [\"Faster cache format for snapshot decode\", \"−0.35 to −0.46 s per warm command\", \"est\", \"needs a design\"],\n  [\"Small: reuse source prep, cheaper sort and gzip, parallel similarity\", \"up to −1.5 s per cold build\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n];\nfunction renderProcs(list, id) {\n  const host = document.getElementById(id);\n  for (const p of list) {\n    const sum = p.steps.reduce((a, s) => a + s[1], 0);\n    const el = document.createElement(\"div\");\n    el.className = \"proc\";\n    el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"proc-head\"><h3>${p.name}</h3><span class=\"total${p.slow ? \" slow\" : \"\"}\">${p.total}</span></div>\n      <div class=\"bar\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"${p.steps.map(s => s[0] + \" \" + fmt(s[1])).join(\", \")}\">${p.steps.map(s => `<div class=\"seg\" style=\"width:${(s[1] / sum * 100).toFixed(2)}%;background:var(--step-${s[2]})\" title=\"${s[0]}: ${fmt(s[1])}\"></div>`).join(\"\")}</div>\n      <div class=\"legend\">${p.steps.map(s => `<span><i style=\"background:var(--step-${s[2]})\"></i>${s[0]} <b>${fmt(s[1])}</b> · ${Math.round(s[1] / sum * 100)}%</span>`).join(\"\")}</div>\n      <div class=\"note\">${p.note}</div>`;\n    host.appendChild(el);\n  }\n}\nfunction renderFixes(list, id) {\n  const host = document.getElementById(id);\n  list.forEach((f, i) => {\n    const tr = document.createElement(\"tr\");\n    tr.innerHTML = `<td class=\"num\">${i + 1}</td><td>${f[0]}</td><td>${f[1]} ${PILL[f[2]]}</td><td class=\"note\">${f[3]}</td>`;\n    host.appendChild(tr);\n  });\n}\n'''\na=s.index('const procs = document.getElementById(\"brain-procs\");')\nb=s.index('const tabs = [')\ns=s[:a]+js+'renderProcs(BRAIN, \"brain-procs\");\\nrenderFixes(FIXES, \"brain-fixes\");\\nrenderProcs(GRAPH, \"graph-procs\");\\nrenderFixes(GFIXES, \"graph-fixes\");\\n\\n'+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('<p class=\"sub\">Every step inside each Entire Graph and Brain process, timed on the latest <span class=\"mono\">main</span>, with the fixes that would speed each one up. Bars are drawn to scale within each process.</p>',\n '<p class=\"sub\">Every step inside each Entire Graph and Brain process, timed on the latest <span class=\"mono\">main</span>, with the fixes that would speed each one up. Bars are drawn to scale within each process. Both fix lists were checked against the source by a second agent before any work started.</p>')\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nnode -e \"const fs=require('fs');const h=fs.readFileSync('/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html','utf8');const js=h.split('<script>')[1].split('</script>')[0];new Function(js);console.log('js parses')\"","description":"Fill the artifact Graph tab and check the script parses"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3701,"cache_read_input_tokens":209635,"output_tokens":5099,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":842},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3701,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5099,"cache_read_input_tokens":209635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3701},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01R2ReeUGCfsnG5s7BDyH5pk":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('    <div class=\"pending\">\\n      <h3>Still being measured</h3>')\nj=s.index('</section>',i)\ngraph_html='''    <div class=\"callout\"><b>One exact-name search took 6 minutes.</b> Searching entire-graph for a bare identifier (<span class=\"mono\">SearchRepository</span>) took 355 s, almost all of it in one <span class=\"mono\">git grep</span> with a regex alternation over the whole commit. The same route costs 8 s on cli, where a fixed-string search takes about 40 ms.</div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Overall the new build is much faster after the first call.</b> Warm queries are 2–6x faster. Cold builds are about 1.8x faster and use half the memory. A second worktree reuses the cache. The old build hangs on every graph-building command on the entire-graph repo itself. Two things got slower: the first query in a repo, and warm <span class=\"mono\">def</span>/<span class=\"mono\">neighbors</span>/<span class=\"mono\">impact</span>.</div>\n\n    <h2>Where the time goes</h2>\n    <div class=\"procs\" id=\"graph-procs\"></div>\n\n    <h2>New build vs the 2026-09-18 build (cli repo)</h2>\n    <div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n      <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Old</th><th>New</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Cold index</td><td class=\"num\">20.96 s</td><td class=\"num\">11.23 s</td><td>1.9x faster</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>First query in a repo (cold)</td><td class=\"num\">14.16 s</td><td class=\"num\">16.23 s</td><td><b>slower</b>: builds the complete graph up front</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Warm query, same question</td><td class=\"num\">5.64 s</td><td class=\"num\">3.06 s</td><td>1.8x faster</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Warm query, new question</td><td class=\"num\">16.44 s</td><td class=\"num\">2.63 s</td><td>6.3x faster (old missed the cache)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Query from a second worktree</td><td class=\"num\">13.69 s</td><td class=\"num\">2.42 s</td><td>5.7x faster (cache shared)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Exact-name query</td><td class=\"num\">14.77 s</td><td class=\"num\">11.77 s</td><td>8 s of it is one git grep</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Warm def / neighbors / impact</td><td class=\"num\">0.45 s</td><td class=\"num\">0.66 s</td><td><b>slower</b>: re-sorts history on every cache hit</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Warm edges / snapshot</td><td class=\"num\">20.3 s</td><td class=\"num\">0.29–0.56 s</td><td>36–71x faster (old rebuilt every time)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Three cold queries at once</td><td class=\"num\">16.50 s</td><td class=\"num\">17.25 s</td><td>about the same wall time, but 1 build instead of 3</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Peak memory, cold index</td><td class=\"num\">1,004 MB</td><td class=\"num\">432 MB</td><td>less than half</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>stats (7 days)</td><td class=\"num\">2.63 s</td><td class=\"num\">3.14 s</td><td>slightly slower</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table></div>\n    <p class=\"note\">entire-brain and entiredb show the same pattern. The optional sqlite search store makes the cache 18–27x larger, and it is not faster on every repo.</p>\n\n    <h2>Proposed fixes, by saving</h2>\n    <p class=\"note\">Ranked by saving per working session (one cold query plus about ten warm commands). A reviewer is checking each against the source now. Each fix becomes its own PR, with an old/new timing taken on a quiet machine and a check that output is unchanged.</p>\n    <div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Fix</th><th>Saving</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody id=\"graph-fixes\"></tbody>\n    </table></div>\n\n    <h2>Wrong answers found</h2>\n    <ul class=\"tight\">\n      <li><span class=\"mono\">neighbors</span> misses a function passed as a value, so it reported no callers for one that has them.</li>\n      <li>A spurious duplicate definition makes <span class=\"mono\">impact</span> ambiguous for one symbol.</li>\n      <li>The graph refuses to index a partial clone (<span class=\"mono\">blob:none</span>), which also breaks Brain's code index on the cli repo.</li>\n    </ul>\n  '''\ns=s[:i]+graph_html+s[j:]\ns=s.replace('<span>Compared with <b>the 2026-09-18 nightly</b></span>','<span>Compared with <b>the 2026-09-18 nightly</b></span><span>3 runs each, median; machine partly loaded by other work</span>',1)\njs='''const GRAPH = [\n  { name: \"Exact-name query, entire-graph repo\", total: \"355 s\", slow: true, note: \"One git grep with a regex alternation over the whole commit (the alias route). 338–370 s across 3 runs.\",\n    steps: [[\"git grep preselect\", 345000, \"a\"], [\"Everything else\", 10000, \"e\"]] },\n  { name: \"First query in a repo (cold), cli\", total: \"17.6 s\", slow: true, note: \"Scans file contents to pick candidates, then builds the complete graph anyway.\",\n    steps: [[\"Preselect content scan\", 4220, \"a\"], [\"Complete build\", 11100, \"b\"], [\"Rank\", 970, \"c\"], [\"Save complete cache\", 460, \"d\"], [\"Selective view\", 350, \"d\"], [\"Other\", 500, \"e\"]] },\n  { name: \"Cold index, cli\", total: \"11.7 s\", note: \"Only 2.2 cores busy on average: the ordered pipeline admits 8 files, so one slow file stalls the rest. Regex is 54% of the CPU.\",\n    steps: [[\"Per-file scan\", 7080, \"a\"], [\"Route passes (one thread)\", 1750, \"b\"], [\"Parse\", 750, \"c\"], [\"Similarity\", 590, \"d\"], [\"Save\", 550, \"d\"], [\"Sort, prepare, other\", 980, \"e\"]] },\n  { name: \"Warm query, cli\", total: \"2.9 s\", note: \"Ranking dominates. Each new question also writes a derived cache file.\",\n    steps: [[\"Rank\", 1270, \"a\"], [\"Load cache\", 630, \"b\"], [\"Save selective view\", 500, \"c\"], [\"Select from full\", 230, \"d\"], [\"Preselect\", 180, \"d\"], [\"Other\", 90, \"e\"]] },\n  { name: \"Warm def / neighbors / impact, cli\", total: \"0.66 s\", note: \"Slower than the old 0.45 s: each cache hit re-reads history and re-sorts every relation.\",\n    steps: [[\"Decode cache\", 350, \"a\"], [\"Re-sort history\", 180, \"b\"], [\"Other\", 130, \"e\"]] },\n];\nconst GFIXES = [\n  [\"Exact-name search: use a fixed-string git grep or the cached term index instead of a regex alternation over the commit\", \"8 s (cli) to about 6 min (entire-graph) per bare-name search\", \"big\", \"timing\"],\n  [\"Let the indexing pipeline run ahead of a slow file (wider ordered window)\", \"cold index −29% (cli) to −36% (brain); every cold command\", \"meas\", \"local patch, identical output\"],\n  [\"Skip the preselect content scan on a cold query when the complete build follows anyway\", \"−4.2 to −6.3 s per first query\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n  [\"Stop re-sorting history on every cache hit; merge in place and remember it per commit\", \"−0.15 to −0.2 s per warm command; fixes the slowdown\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n  [\"Stop writing the derived selective view on every new warm question\", \"−0.5 to −0.7 s per warm query\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n  [\"Replace per-pattern regex in relation extraction with one shared pass\", \"−2 to −4 s per cold build\", \"est\", \"CPU profile\"],\n  [\"Run the HTTP route passes inside the parallel scan\", \"−1 to −1.7 s per cold build\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n  [\"Precompute ranking token variants\", \"−0.5 to −1 s per warm query\", \"est\", \"CPU profile\"],\n  [\"Faster cache format for snapshot decode\", \"−0.35 to −0.46 s per warm command\", \"est\", \"needs a design\"],\n  [\"Small: reuse source prep, cheaper sort and gzip, parallel similarity\", \"up to −1.5 s per cold build\", \"est\", \"step map\"],\n];\nfunction renderProcs(list, id) {\n  const host = document.getElementById(id);\n  for (const p of list) {\n    const sum = p.steps.reduce((a, s) => a + s[1], 0);\n    const el = document.createElement(\"div\");\n    el.className = \"proc\";\n    el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"proc-head\"><h3>${p.name}</h3><span class=\"total${p.slow ? \" slow\" : \"\"}\">${p.total}</span></div>\n      <div class=\"bar\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"${p.steps.map(s => s[0] + \" \" + fmt(s[1])).join(\", \")}\">${p.steps.map(s => `<div class=\"seg\" style=\"width:${(s[1] / sum * 100).toFixed(2)}%;background:var(--step-${s[2]})\" title=\"${s[0]}: ${fmt(s[1])}\"></div>`).join(\"\")}</div>\n      <div class=\"legend\">${p.steps.map(s => `<span><i style=\"background:var(--step-${s[2]})\"></i>${s[0]} <b>${fmt(s[1])}</b> · ${Math.round(s[1] / sum * 100)}%</span>`).join(\"\")}</div>\n      <div class=\"note\">${p.note}</div>`;\n    host.appendChild(el);\n  }\n}\nfunction renderFixes(list, id) {\n  const host = document.getElementById(id);\n  list.forEach((f, i) => {\n    const tr = document.createElement(\"tr\");\n    tr.innerHTML = `<td class=\"num\">${i + 1}</td><td>${f[0]}</td><td>${f[1]} ${PILL[f[2]]}</td><td class=\"note\">${f[3]}</td>`;\n    host.appendChild(tr);\n  });\n}\n'''\na=s.index('const procs = document.getElementById(\"brain-procs\");')\nb=s.index('const tabs = [')\ns=s[:a]+js+'renderProcs(BRAIN, \"brain-procs\");\\nrenderFixes(FIXES, \"brain-fixes\");\\nrenderProcs(GRAPH, \"graph-procs\");\\nrenderFixes(GFIXES, \"graph-fixes\");\\n\\n'+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('<p class=\"sub\">Every step inside each Entire Graph and Brain process, timed on the latest <span class=\"mono\">main</span>, with the fixes that would speed each one up. Bars are drawn to scale within each process.</p>',\n '<p class=\"sub\">Every step inside each Entire Graph and Brain process, timed on the latest <span class=\"mono\">main</span>, with the fixes that would speed each one up. Bars are drawn to scale within each process. Both fix lists were checked against the source by a second agent before any work started.</p>')\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nnode -e \"const fs=require('fs');const h=fs.readFileSync('/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html','utf8');const js=h.split('<script>')[1].split('</script>')[0];new Function(js);console.log('js parses')\"","description":"Fill the artifact Graph tab and check the script parses"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c6ab0acd-450c-4a4a-8387-a9811ba21e2b","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMWv5Em9yCCc1ZHsBATY","requestRef":"eabda28c-c1de-4fe9-9667-1002a718843d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1dd7f3f4-e872-4347-8b43-90d87e37c61e","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:14:45.193Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-f