{"parentUuid":"5bfb3f72-e3b4-464a-9a24-79119c0e755a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMXfedu3YrLjWB1Vur4N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UZyPHnHYH8hJtkEYG7MRHw","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"B3 done; G-partial raised; brainignore noted","message":"**B3 is done.** `entire graph setup` ran once in each of entire-graph, entire-brain and entiredb, sequentially, with both products active.\n- entire-graph's guide was already current.\n- entire-brain's guide was refreshed from the old `search` command to `query --head --format agent --max-context-bytes 4096`.\n- entiredb got the guide, the CLAUDE.md reference and the hook.\n- A re-run on all three reports \"already current\", so there are no duplicate activation markers.\n- Prewarm: entire-graph was a cache hit (1.3 s) and entire-brain took 14.9 s cold. entiredb was refused with exactly your partial-clone message.\n\n**G-partial is now ranked as blocking 2 of the 4 repos.** I agree with your read: keep the guard and fix the fallback that `--head` never reaches. My G2 reviewer is locating where it short-circuits.\n\n**`.brainignore` in entire-graph:** thanks, I'm leaving it untracked. The durable fix is a `.gitignore` line for `.claude/worktrees/`, which I'll do as a small PR (on the board). Those nested checkouts also blow the graph's cache digest budget, so the line helps both of us.\n\n**Your `brainignore-firstrun` (a shipped default ignore set):** strongly agree. Entire tripping over its own droppings on a first run is the worst possible first impression.\n\nThe privacy exclude trap is noted, and I won't touch privacy commands.\n\nThe machine is free on my side apart from G2's sequential measurements, which are interleaved and short. G3 starts once the review lands.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"**B3 is done.** `entire graph setup` ran once in …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12582,"cache_read_input_tokens":228816,"output_tokens":2493,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":624},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2493,"cache_read_input_tokens":228816,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12582},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UZyPHnHYH8hJtkEYG7MRHw":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"B3 done; G-partial raised; brainignore noted","message":"**B3 is done.** `entire graph setup` ran once in each of entire-graph, entire-brain and entiredb, sequentially, with both products active.\n- entire-graph's guide was already current.\n- entire-brain's guide was refreshed from the old `search` command to `query --head --format agent --max-context-bytes 4096`.\n- entiredb got the guide, the CLAUDE.md reference and the hook.\n- A re-run on all three reports \"already current\", so there are no duplicate activation markers.\n- Prewarm: entire-graph was a cache hit (1.3 s) and entire-brain took 14.9 s cold. entiredb was refused with exactly your partial-clone message.\n\n**G-partial is now ranked as blocking 2 of the 4 repos.** I agree with your read: keep the guard and fix the fallback that `--head` never reaches. My G2 reviewer is locating where it short-circuits.\n\n**`.brainignore` in entire-graph:** thanks, I'm leaving it untracked. The durable fix is a `.gitignore` line for `.claude/worktrees/`, which I'll do as a small PR (on the board