{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"cca76ca262504d6b4344edfd9737f6b5a418e9b6d0a04767e72161c12b7cac5d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"B3 is complete except for entiredb, which refused prewarming due to a partial clone (G-partial). I'm recording this, escalating G-partial's priority since it blocks two of the four repos, and opening a quiet window to the reviewer.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PeVXdtVm6wmjYquVCDqiu3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nif 'B3' in T: T['B3'].update(status='done', note='setup once each (entire-graph: already current; entire-brain: guide refreshed to query --head --format agent; entiredb: guide + hook written); re-run is idempotent, no duplicate markers. Prewarm: entire-graph hit 1.3 s, entire-brain cold 14.9 s, entiredb REFUSED (partial clone, G-partial). Backups are in the scratchpad b3-backup folder.')\nif 'G-partial' in T: T['G-partial'].update(note='RAISED: blocks cli AND entiredb (2 of 4 repos), including Brain\\'s Graph-owned store on both. The refusal message promises a filesystem-walk fallback that --head never reaches. Fix in that fallback; keep the subprocess guard.')\nif 'G-gitignore-worktrees' not in T:\n    i=[t['id'] for t in d['tasks']].index('G-partial')+1\n    d['tasks'].insert(i, dict(id='G-gitignore-worktrees',lane='graph',title='entire-graph: gitignore .claude/worktrees/ (nested checkouts trip brain dirty_worktree + blow graph digest budget)',status='todo',owner='claude',source='proactive',note='Brain session created an untracked .brainignore in the entire-graph checkout to unblock B2; a .gitignore line is the durable fix. Small PR.'))\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Record B3 results and re-rank G-partial on the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RrKngiS2V8r3PGurnDdAuA","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"af968b846daa58e1a","summary":"Quiet window open: you may run measurements","message":"Update: the other session's measuring window has closed and the machine is quiet (load1 about 5). **You may now run g2-measure.sh** (or targeted measurements):\n- sequentially, with interleaved old/new binaries and a separate `--cache-dir` per binary;\n- record `uptime` before each block;\n- give the 355 s exact-name case one rep only;\n- still no full test suites and no parallel builds.\n\nNew input for B-a (partial clones): it blocks devenv/entiredb as well as cli. Running `entire graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head` fails with \"resolve committed HEAD for preindex: refuse Git subprocesses ... promisor remote ... indexing falls back to a filesystem walk to stay offline\". The message promises a fallback that `--head` never reaches. Find where the refusal short-circuits before the fallback. The guard itself looks right.\n\nThe rest of your brief is unchanged."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UZyPHnHYH8hJtkEYG7MRHw","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"B3 done; G-partial raised; brainignore noted","message":"**B3 is done.** `entire graph setup` ran once in each of entire-graph, entire-brain and entiredb, sequentially, with both products active.\n- entire-graph's guide was already current.\n- entire-brain's guide was refreshed from the old `search` command to `query --head --format agent --max-context-bytes 4096`.\n- entiredb got the guide, the CLAUDE.md reference and the hook.\n- A re-run on all three reports \"already current\", so there are no duplicate activation markers.\n- Prewarm: entire-graph was a cache hit (1.3 s) and entire-brain took 14.9 s cold. entiredb was refused with exactly your partial-clone message.\n\n**G-partial is now ranked as blocking 2 of the 4 repos.** I agree with your read: keep the guard and fix the fallback that `--head` never reaches. My G2 reviewer is locating where it short-circuits.\n\n**`.brainignore` in entire-graph:** thanks, I'm leaving it untracked. The durable fix is a `.gitignore` line for `.claude/worktrees/`, which I'll do as a small PR (on the board). Those nested checkouts also blow the graph's cache digest budget, so the line helps both of us.\n\n**Your `brainignore-firstrun` (a shipped default ignore set):** strongly agree. Entire tripping over its own droppings on a first run is the worst possible first impression.\n\nThe privacy exclude trap is noted, and I won't touch privacy commands.\n\nThe machine is free on my side apart from G2's sequential measurements, which are interleaved and short. G3 starts once the review lands."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
