{"parentUuid":"00e0b54d-2f75-4bf2-a55c-d170df2d39cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMZt97yEc9DQCfRoE2td","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing one shared protocol file for every fix agent, so each brief stays short and the rules stay identical:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4553,"cache_read_input_tokens":252866,"output_tokens":2298,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":130},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4553,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2298,"cache_read_input_tokens":252866,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4553},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1943903f-fd9c-4a96-9dc9-e46d7c010077","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMZt8QJz7Cv9h9z3XvmC","requestRef":"4dd84f65-4ebd-4a07-b04b-76566ad47948","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9351c678-34bf-4f62-8969-9ccc3acfd1ca","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:53:02.718Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"9351c678-34bf-4f62-8969-9ccc3acfd1ca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMZt97yEc9DQCfRoE2td","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014Et2eQ5zaw7pJJS4rDiSDL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md","content":"# G3 fix protocol (entire-graph speed and correctness fixes)\n\nEvery G3 fix agent follows this file. The item-specific brief comes in the agent's prompt.\n\n## Inputs\n- Fix list: `GRAPH-SPEEDUPS.md`. Review, which is authoritative where it disagrees: `GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`.\n- Step maps: `PROCESS-MAP.md`, `stepmaps/`. Reviewer tools: `g2-measure.sh`, `g2-strip.py`, `g2-patterns/`, `g2-v2/`, `raw/g2/`.\n- All of these live in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/`.\n\n## Workspace\n- One fresh worktree per fix, off `origin/main`:\n  `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin main && git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph worktree add -b <branch> /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-<short-name> origin/main`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph` is a main checkout. Read from it; never edit, commit, or switch branches there.\n- No `git stash`: one stash is shared across all worktrees, and parallel agents collide.\n- Commit with the repo's configured identity. **Never** pass `-c user.email=...` or `--author`.\n- Conventional commit subject (`perf(sem): ...`, `fix(cli): ...`). **No AI or Claude attribution lines** in commits or PR bodies. No references to people or conversations.\n\n## Tools: graph and brain first\n1. Preflight once:\n   - `entire graph version --json`, `entire graph capabilities --json`\n   - `entire brain version`, `entire brain capabilities --json`\n2. Before editing any exported or shared symbol, run `entire graph impact --repo <worktree> --head --symbol <Name>` and cite the result. Use `def` and `neighbors --direction in` for callers. grep only supplements; it never replaces these.\n3. For why code exists or prior decisions, run `entire brain recall \"<question>\" --json` from `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph`. An empty result is not proof.\n\n## CPU, measuring and coordination\n- Other agents run in parallel on this machine. **Any timing run, cold index, or test run longer than about a minute must hold the measure lock:**\n  `flock /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/measure.lock -c '<command>'`\n  Keep each locked block short (minutes, not an hour) so the others are not starved.\n- Before a timing block, check two things:\n  - `uptime`: record load1. Don't measure above about 8.\n  - `/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json`: any row with `\"lane\": \"brain\"`, `\"status\": \"doing\"` and a title starting `measuring:` means wait until it clears.\n- Focused tests: `env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./<pkg> -run '<Regex>' -count=1`. The shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3, which breaks colour-assert tests on correct code.\n- **No full local suites.** CI runs them. Exception: the package you changed may be run whole, under the lock, with `-p 1`.\n- Never `--daemon`, `entire brain setup` or `entire brain refresh`. Never touch `~/.local/share/entire`.\n\n## Before/after timing (speed fixes)\n- Build two binaries: `go build -o /tmp-free path` into your worktree's `bin/`. One from `origin/main` (base), one from your branch.\n- Interleave base/new runs. Use a separate `--cache-dir` per binary, and a fresh one per cold run. 3 reps, report the median. Use the same repos as the study (clones under `timing/repos/`, or `/Users/suhaan/devenv/{entire-graph,entire-brain}`).\n- **Output identity:** compare base vs new JSON outputs byte-for-byte after `g2-strip.py` (it strips timing fields), or the snapshot sha256. If the output is meant to change, say exactly how and test it.\n- The index cache is keyed by tree, not binary, so base and new must never share a cache dir.\n\n## Tests: mutation-proven\n- Add or adjust a test that pins the new behaviour.\n- **Verified by weakening:** temporarily break the guard or fix, show the test goes red (paste the failing line), then restore it and verify the restore by `git diff`.\n- A test that cannot go red is not a test.\n- Watch the Windows traps: filepath separators, CRLF checkouts, and platform branches that nothing executes.\n\n## PR\n- `git push -u origin <branch>`, then `gh pr create --repo entireio/entire-graph --base main`.\n- Body sections:\n  - **Summary:** what and why.\n  - **Measurements:** a base vs new table with medians, reps, load1, repos, and the identity check.\n  - **Test plan:** the tests, and what you weakened to prove them.\n- Do NOT merge, approve, request reviewers, or create an Entire trail by hand.\n- Watch CI with `gh pr checks <n> --repo entireio/entire-graph`. Fix real failures.\n  - A running check has conclusion `\"\"`. It has not failed.\n  - `test (macos-latest)` near 20 minutes is usually the suite timeout, not your diff. Check the log before changing code.\n- If an Entire Gates agent review posts findings on the trail, address the real ones: fix the code, or explain in a PR comment.\n\n## Report (caveman-ultra, ≤ 40 lines)\nInclude:\n- the PR number and branch;\n- the base → new medians with load;\n- the identity check result;\n- the tests and the weakening proof;\n- CI state, enumerated as green, failed, or running;\n- anything you could not finish, and why.\n\nUse RTK for shell (auto-rewritten; `rtk proxy <cmd>` for raw).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4553,"cache_read_input_tokens":252866,"output_tokens":2298,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":130},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4553,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2298,"cache_read_input_tokens":252866,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4553},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014Et2eQ5zaw7pJJS4rDiSDL":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md","content":"# G3 fix protocol (entire-graph speed and correctness fixes)\n\nEvery G3 fix agent follows this file. The item-specific brief comes in the agent's prompt.\n\n## Inputs\n- Fix list: `GRAPH-SPEEDUPS.md`. Review, which is authoritative where it disagrees: `GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`.\n- Step maps: `PROCESS-MAP.md`, `stepmaps/`. Reviewer tools: `g2-measure.sh`, `g2-strip.py`, `g2-patterns/`, `g2-v2/`, `raw/g2/`.\n- All of these live in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/`.\n\n## Workspace\n- One fresh worktree per fix, off `origin/main`:\n  `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin main && git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph worktree add -b <branch> /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-<short-name> origin/main`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph` is a main checkout. Read from it; never edit, commit, or switch branches there.\n- No `git stash`: one stash is shared across all worktrees, and parallel agents collide.\n- Commit with the repo's configured identity. **Never** pass `-c user.email=...` or `--author`.\n- Conventional commit subject (`perf(sem): ...`, `fix(cli): ...`). **No AI or Claude attribution lines** in commits or PR bodies. No references to people or conversations.\n\n## Tools: graph and brain first\n1. Preflight once:\n   - `entire graph version --json`, `entire graph capabilities --json`\n   - `entire brain version`, `entire brain capabilities --json`\n2. Before editing any exported or shared symbol, run `entire graph impact --repo <worktree> --head --symbol <Name>` and cite the result. Use `def` and `neighbors --direction in` for callers. grep only supplements; it never replaces these.\n3. For why code exists or prior decisions, run `entire brain recall \"<question>\" --json` from `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph`. An empty result is not proof.\n\n## CPU, measuring and coordination\n- Other agents run in parallel on this machine. **Any timing run, cold index, or test run longer than about a minute must hold the measure lock:**\n  `flock /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/measure.lock -c '<command>'`\n  Keep each locked block short (minutes, not an hour) so the others are not starved.\n- Before a timing block, check two things:\n  - `uptime`: record load1. Don't measure above about 8.\n  - `/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json`: any row with `\"lane\": \"brain\"`, `\"status\": \"doing\"` and a title starting `measuring:` means wait until it clears.\n- Focused tests: `env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./<pkg> -run '<Regex>' -count=1`. The shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3, which breaks colour-assert tests on correct code.\n- **No full local suites.** CI runs them. Exception: the package you changed may be run whole, under the lock, with `-p 1`.\n- Never `--daemon`, `entire brain setup` or `entire brain refresh`. Never touch `~/.local/share/entire`.\n\n## Before/after timing (speed fixes)\n- Build two binaries: `go build -o /tmp-free path` into your worktree's `bin/`. One from `origin/main` (base), one from your branch.\n- Interleave base/new runs. Use a separate `--cache-dir` per binary, and a fresh one per cold run. 3 reps, report the median. Use the same repos as the study (clones under `timing/repos/`, or `/Users/suhaan/devenv/{entire-graph,entire-brain}`).\n- **Output identity:** compare base vs new JSON outputs byte-for-byte after `g2-strip.py` (it strips timing fields), or the snapshot sha256. If the output is meant to change, say exactly how and test it.\n- The index cache is keyed by tree, not binary, so base and new must never share a cache dir.\n\n## Tests: mutation-proven\n- Add or adjust a test that pins the new behaviour.\n- **Verified by weakening:** temporarily break the guard or fix, show the test goes red (paste the failing line), then restore it and verify the restore by `git diff`.\n- A test that cannot go red is not a test.\n- Watch the Windows traps: filepath separators, CRLF checkouts, and platform branches that nothing executes.\n\n## PR\n- `git push -u origin <branch>`, then `gh pr create --repo entireio/entire-graph --base main`.\n- Body sections:\n  - **Summary:** what and why.\n  - **Measurements:** a base vs new table with medians, reps, load1, repos, and the identity check.\n  - **Test plan:** the tests, and what you weakened to prove them.\n- Do NOT merge, approve, request reviewers, or create an Entire trail by hand.\n- Watch CI with `gh pr checks <n> --repo entireio/entire-graph`. Fix real failures.\n  - A running check has conclusion `\"\"`. It has not failed.\n  - `test (macos-latest)` near 20 minutes is usually the suite timeout, not your diff. Check the log before changing code.\n- If an Entire Gates agent review posts findings on the trail, address the real ones: fix the code, or explain in a PR comment.\n\n## Report (caveman-ultra, ≤ 40 lines)\nInclude:\n- the PR number and branch;\n- the base → new medians with load;\n- the identity check result;\n- the tests and the weakening proof;\n- CI state, enumerated as green, failed, or running;\n- anything you could not finish, and why.\n\nUse RTK for shell (auto-rewritten; `rtk proxy <cmd>` for raw).\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1943903f-fd9c-4a96-9dc9-e46d7c010077","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMZt8QJz7Cv9h9z3XvmC","requestRef":"4dd84f65-4ebd-4a07-b04b-76566ad47948","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d99ff45-f309-4d0e-ba75-45a1b4d64237","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:53:22.419Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":