{"parentUuid":"b850492f-e2ce-4837-a56c-4268ea6899ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMaPqj49GNfL8PhTDcLx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KTNEcfFdWaeDSx3Q1ptmbi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"f=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test.md; python3 - \"$f\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p).read()\na='''**Why:** both look identical'''\nadd='''3. **The fixture never exercised the guard (2026-10-24).** I specified a \"weaken\n   GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH\" proof on a `git clone --filter=blob:none file://` clone. Locally that clone\n   still receives every blob, so nothing is missing, no lazy fetch is possible, and removing the\n   guard \"changes nothing\", which I had wired to \"stop and report what really protects us\".\n   A peer caught it before the agent ran it. A second confound: two guards\n   (`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH`, `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=`) each block the fetch independently, so removing one\n   with the other still set also \"changes nothing\". Working fixture: clone normally, set\n   `remote.origin.promisor`, repack without the blob, then verify `--missing=print` shows 1.\n\n'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a, add+a)\nb='''- when a mutation doesn't fire, first prove'''\nassert s.count(b)==1\ns=s.replace(b,'''- **before specifying a weakening, prove the fixture reaches the guarded path**: a missing object\n  really is missing, a counter-case really fires without the guard (the \"no guards\" row must\n  succeed). Remove ONE guard at a time when several overlap, and assert exit code + stderr.\n'''+b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nsed -i '' 's#^- \\[Mutation didn.t fire? Suspect the test\\](mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test.md) — .*#- [Mutation didn'\"'\"'t fire? Suspect the test](mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test.md) — fixture missing, empty, or never reached the guard (blob:none file:// clone ke